			"notes": {
				"rationale": "hinauszulaufen is the zu-infinitive of separable hinauslaufen, written as one word with zu between the particle hinaus and the stem. The word is a Fusion of hinaus, zu and laufen: the VERB attests its particle and stem pieces, [hinaus, laufen], and the zu piece is PART zu, as a zu written apart would be (de/fused-word-pieces, de/bare-infinitive-zu). It is one VERB target, not a directional adverb beside laufen. Ruled on #743 (BT-A3, A7)."
			},
